<title>USA: U.S. steel imports up six percent in Jan to Sept.</title>
<headline>U.S. steel imports up six percent in Jan to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>In the first nine months of the year, the United States imported 20,662,961 net tons of steel mill products, up 6.1 percent on the same period last year, the American Iron and Steel Institute reported.</p>
<p>September imports were 2,683,493 tons, down 9.5 percent from August, but up 67.1 percent from the 1,605,538 tons imported in September 1995.</p>
<p>September imports account for 25.3 percent of apparent consumption, up 18 percent from a year earlier and down from 27 percent in August 1996.</p>
<p>Year to date imports represented 22.4 percent of apparent consumption.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
